"I was watching my childhood\nWhen I saw them playing\nOn a ground of new-felt joy\nNo restrictions and they were enjoying\n\nSaw what I was a vollyball\nUsed as a basket one\nThey were enjoying the moment\nAnd that was enough fun\n\nI saw a group playing volley\nThey didn't know the rules\nNeither they had the skills for it\nAnd they didn't care less\n\nAnother group played, on the same ground\nIt was a handball, used differently\nIt was a game of catch\nAnd they were so happy\n\nOne ball came to me\nIt missed my face though\nThought I could return it\nThen remembered the past of mine\n\nI ain't good at the sport myself\nBut surely more capable then them\nThought I could teach them some\nThen remembered, my own childhood\n\nI was like them, they're better though\nDidn't know how to play, but wanted to\nDidn't had the stamina, yet enjoyed the game\nDidn't had any restrictions, never wanted one as well \n\nNever wanted one to interfere\nIn the game I played with my friends\nNever wanted one to lecture\nIn the game where fun never ends\n\nI know they'll learn soon enough\nAnd will cherish the memories as I do\nShould I teach them today the game\nAnd they'll never have the mistakes to do\n\nWon't they enjoy the stupid actions\nNever will experience those self made rules\nThey'll lose their childhood freedom\nWhich was beyond, those formal rules\n\nLet them enjoy the way they do\nI had my childhood, so they do\nLet them create some memories too\nWhich they'll cherish, by seeing what I saw through"